{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1329934-what-do-reapers-do-in-the-underworld","id":1329934,"title":"What do Reapers do in the Underworld?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-08-08T11:17:52-07:00","id":1329934,"title":"What do Reapers do in the Underworld?","content":"Like I say in the topic, what do Reapers do in the Underworld. There's mention of them sweeping over River Cities in the Underworld section and it's implied they get up to bad stuff, but later in their section it seems like they are relatively benevolent. I was just reading the Geist style guide and they are described as harassing the dead in the Underworld. I'm pretty sure its not really ever explained in the book, but has there been any discussion from developers or writers that sheds more light on it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/565-therian","name":"Therian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar565_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-08T12:25:46-07:00","id":1329951,"title":"","content":"As they are individuals i suppose it depends on their take about the chtonic mythology.<br /> Sone could take on a priest role and perform religious rites, other could torment the sinful souls or comfort them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-08-13T04:47:35-07:00","id":1330727,"title":"","content":"Yeah I mean, one of the main benefits of doning a death mask and becoming a Reaper it's because you become an insanely powerful ghost, much stronger than most ghosts that exist in the great below, so it really comes in a certain point to the Reaper's own motives and goals that they probably coudln't reach as a common ghost. Maybe the Reaper wants to get revenge on a merchant king of some river city that abused her when she was weaker, maybe she wants to search for more death masks to create some sort of reaper guild, etc.<br /> <br /> I get this feeling that whatever malicious intelligence rules the Underworld chooses really well which ghosts might encounter a death mask and become a Reaper, like, there's not explicitly said, but whenever the book describes a ghost finding a death mask &quot;by chance&quot;, to me there's always this vibe of something calculated. My point is that it seems that ghosts who are really desperate or who don't see the underworld as all that bad are the ones more likely to come across a death mask, and that means that they're already more or less likely to abuse other ghosts, the death mask just gives them the final push in that direction giving them ghostly superpowers.<br /> <br /> Also what Neos01 said makes total sense, most Reapers will also have something to say on the cthonic gods who rule the great below, and how all ghosts belong down there, it's an obsession that really consumes them, and the way other ghosts react to this preaching might say a lot about a Reaper and what they do in the Underrworld to expand the cthonic mythos. Maybe the reaper lash out and destroy ghosts blaspheming agaisn't the cthonic gods ir who scheme together with Sin-Eater Krewes; maybe she's a genuinely charismatic Reaper and really convince other ghosts of the &quot;true&quot; doctrine of the cthonic gods (they sound way more dangerous when other ghosts actually believe and support them), she might act as some force of nature keeping track of some river cities and wrecking things up whenever some river city starts to get more confortable and stable or when they openly help Sin-Eaters and so on","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25516-pinkhaunt","name":"PinkHaunt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25516_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T13:28:26-08:00","id":1355686,"title":"","content":"At it\u2019s most basic, when they aren\u2019t Reaping, they could be doing any sorts of things, in a very Villain\u2019s Gone Shopping sort of way. The Cthonic Gods might influence them to accomplish certain goals, or they might be utterly silent and the Reaper in question goes off to do something they believe their God will approve.<br /> <br /> They could also try to do the unthinkable: try to make things better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-28T21:52:19-08:00","id":1363908,"title":"","content":"The sense I get from the Underworld in 2e is that everything about it kinda forces you downward. Not just the rivers themselves, but the whole underworld seems to be designed to funnel ghosts deeper and deeper into the endless ocean. So I kinda imagine Reapers as part of that dynamic. If a ghostly town or congregation gets too stable, they destabilize it, probably violently. They harass and hound ghosts that they find into running deeper in. Maybe they kill/discorporate/whatever-the-term-is one or two of them, but only to show that they aren't fucking around.<br /> <br /> A good way to think of it is that the Underworld is a prison, and Reapers have found a way to stay their sentence by becoming the wardens. When they're in the underworld, they're enforcing order and making sure the prisoners serve their sentences properly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10984-neckbeard-the-pirate","name":"Neckbeard the Pirate","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T00:25:01-08:00","id":1363926,"title":"","content":"I'll probably reread it but the vibe I got was either they are like, insane to the point that they don't realize they're a reaper until they get the call for their hunt. Or they 'live' sort of like the Seers. Prestige positions from twisted and cruel gods in exchange for loyalty and ghosts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-29T04:57:21-08:00","id":1363946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1329934-what-do-reapers-do-in-the-underworld?p=1363926#post1363926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll probably reread it but the vibe I got was either they are like, insane to the point that they don't realize they're a reaper until they get the call for their hunt. Or they 'live' sort of like the Seers. Prestige positions from twisted and cruel gods in exchange for loyalty and ghosts.</div> </div> </div> </div>The latter is definitely true. Which isn't to say the former don't exist, but they're a minority.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}